Z||000000||DreXteR||03-19-2001||11:06 PM||||Hi, I need a quick answer in this. From wich v8 are the piston rods that fits in a 3.4 camero???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  Need exact info(make, model, measures, everithing....PLEASE  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ), I have a source that can sell me a set of those for my project rebuild. <P><BR>Thanx<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||03-19-2001||11:45 PM||||SBC, but they need to be narrowed. Don't bother.<P>And I quote (myself as paraphrased from the Chevy Power Book):<P>"The 5.7L rods are the same length as the 2.8L. However, they must be narrowed to fit. But the 2.8L rods are totally acceptable for less than 7000rpm use."<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 03-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||lou_dias||03-20-2001||01:12 AM||||No they are not.  I think some article goes on to say that you can get V8 bearings as well.  I spun the bearings on my original 2.8 then rebuilt to a 3.1...<BR>Then threw a rod through the block on a camaro 3.4 with 14k miles and I just did it again on another rebuilt 3.4 with 24k miles.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DreXteR||03-20-2001||07:47 AM||||So, the rods from small block works w/o modification in a 3.4 setup? I will talk to my friend for more info about the rods to post it here to be 100% sure that will work.<P>Thanx<P><BR>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||03-20-2001||08:21 AM||||DreXter,<P>Read again. You need to "narrow" the SBC rod to make it work. You also need to use the "small jounal" rods from early motors such as the 327 CU-IN.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||03-20-2001||01:53 PM||||Get the GM Chevy Power Book at the Chevy dealership's part counter. <P>It states that the 660 rods are good to 7000 RPM. If GM is wrong, GM is wrong. There is no value to putting SBC rods in a 660 unless you plan on something horrifingly unstreetable. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||DreXteR||03-20-2001||11:24 PM||||Well, I plan to use a T60 @ 16psi, thats why the need of forged rods.  <P>The crank from the camaro engine will handle such power??? <P>The Hypernoutics can be used in a Turbo setup??????<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000007||lou_dias||03-21-2001||09:12 AM||||take my advice, it's the rods and bearings that are the weak links on the v6's...I've gone through 4 engines.  2 bearings went bad, rod knock, on the other 2, rods let go<P>do whatever you can to get beeier rods and better bearings||||reg||1
Z||000008||DreXteR||03-21-2001||10:19 AM||||Thanx for the advise lou.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||03-21-2001||11:39 AM||||Get the Chevy Power Book, the details are in there.<P>Boy, snapping a 660 rod takes some effort. I know that GM found a #4 rod bearing problem but breaking them doesn't seem to be a common occurance. What conditions caused it?||||reg||1
